  data: {
    LLM: "Bid according to hand strength and trump potential; remember card ranking (5, J, A♥, then K-Q and numerals; red suits 'highest best', black 'lowest best'). The 5 of trump and J of trump are the top trumps; A of hearts is always trump.\n\nCompeting with dealer: dealer can take by equalling, so bids can be pushed up. Holding the highest trump gives +5; time when you play it. In 110, reaching the target in the same deal—who took tricks first can decide the winner.\n\nBid 60 only when you can win all five tricks. If you bid lower and make all tricks you score 30 (five tricks + highest trump), not 60. Track who is close to 110 and whether to bid to win or to block.",
    Player: "Bid according to hand strength and trump potential; remember card ranking (5, J, A♥, then K-Q and numerals; red suits 'highest best', black 'lowest best'). The 5 of trump and J of trump are the top trumps; A of hearts is always trump.\n\nCompeting with dealer: dealer can take by equalling, so bids can be pushed up. Holding the highest trump gives +5; time when you play it. In 110, reaching the target in the same deal—who took tricks first can decide the winner.\n\nBid 60 only when you can win all five tricks. If you bid lower and make all tricks you score 30 (five tricks + highest trump), not 60. Track who is close to 110 and whether to bid to win or to block.",
